messages:    6%|5         | 33/600 [02:10<05:48,  1.63it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nConscientiousness is high on most firms' list of traits they want in employees. Yet a recent study found that laid-off conscientious individuals are less likely to find jobs within five months than are their peers who shirked their workplace responsibilities.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, each of the following, if true, helps to resolve the apparent paradox above EXCEPT:\n# Options:\nA) People who shirk their workplace responsibilities are less likely to keep the jobs they have, so there are more of them looking for jobs.\nB) Finding a job is less urgent for the conscientious, because they tend to have larger savings.\nC) Conscientious people tend to have a greater than average concern with finding the job most suited to their interests and abilities.\nD) Resentment about having been laid off in spite of their conscientiousness leads some people to perform poorly in interviews.", '<think>.\nTo resolve the apparent paradox, we need to consider the options and see which one does not help to explain why laid-off conscientious individuals are less likely to find jobs within five months than their peers who shirked their workplace responsibilities.\n\nOption A suggests that people who shirk their workplace responsibilities are less likely to keep the jobs they have, so there are more of them looking for jobs.This could explain why laid-off conscientious individuals are less likely to find jobs, as they may have fewer job opportunities due to their conscientiousness.\n\nOption B suggests that finding a job is less urgent for the conscientious, because they tend to have larger savings.This could also explain why laid-off conscientious individuals are less likely to find jobs, as they may not need to find a job as urgently as their peers who shirked their responsibilities.Option D suggests that individuals who were laid off due to their conscientiousness may perform poorly in interviews as a result of their resentment, which could explain why they are more motivated to excel in interviews.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
