messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nThe principle of utmost good faith in insurance means that both parties to the insurance must be honest and trustworthy during the entire process of signing and performing the insurance contract, abide by the trust with the utmost sincerity, truthfully inform important information, do not deceive or conceal, and ensure the correct performance of their respective rights And obligations.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, in which of the following, the applicant has not fulfilled the principle of utmost good faith?\n# Options:\nA) Liu took a medical leave due to liver cancer. in july 2005, liu's decoration company insured group life insurance for all employees of the company. when the company submitted the list of insureds, it stated in the column of health status that liu took a leave of liver cancer. condition\nB) Mr. zhang, in good health, has purchased a simple life insurance under the collective organization of the unit, and fills in the word health in the column health of the insured on the insurance application form\nC) In the new semester, the school asked freshmen to pay an insurance premium of 25 yuan each, of which student safety insurance was 10 yuan, and additional disease insurance was 15 yuan. on september 8, a new student zhang had abdominal pain and was diagnosed with a congenital disease by the hospital. zhang was hospitalized, and zhang's father asked the insurance company to reimburse the medical expenses\nD) Li was hospitalized with gastric cancer, was discharged after the operation, and went to work normally. later, li was introduced by someone to insured for simple life insurance, and when filling out the insurance form, he did not declare the fact that he was suffering from cancer", "<think>.\nTo determine which option does not fulfill the principle of utmost good faith, we need to analyze each option individually and see if the applicant has provided accurate and truthful information about their health status.\n\nA) Liu took a medical leave due to liver cancer.In July 2005, Liu's decoration company insured group life insurance for all employees of the company.When the company submitted the list of insureds, it stated in the column of health status that Liu took a leave of liver cancer.Condition.\n\nIn this case, Liu took a medical leave due to liver cancer, which is a truthful statement.Therefore, Liu has fulfilled the principle of utmost good faith.\n\nB) Mr. Zhang, in good health, has purchased a simple life insurance under the collective organization of the unit, and fills in the word health in the column health of the insured on the insurance application form.\n\nIn this case, Mr. Zhang is in good health, which is a truthful statement.Therefore, Mr. Zhang has fulfilled the principle of utmost good faith.\n\nC) In the new semester, the school asked freshmen to pay an insurance premium of 25 yuan each, of which student safety insurance was 10 yuan, and additional disease insurance was 15 yuan.On September 8, a new student Zhang had abdominal pain and was diagnosed with a congenital disease by the hospital.Zhang was hospitalized, and Zhang's father asked the insurance company to reimburse the medical expenses.In this case, Li was never hospitalized with gastric cancer, and he always declared the fact that he was suffering from cancer when filling out the insurance form.Therefore, Li has not violated the principle of utmost good faith.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
