messages:   24%|##4       | 146/600 [09:07<02:23,  3.17it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nThe subtext is originally a dramatic word, which refers to an opinion that is actually contained in the line but not clearly stated. Rich subtext can often make the performance more intriguing.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, based on the above definition, which statement contains a typical subtext?\n# Options:\nA) When giving a lecture, the history teacher said: china is a land of etiquette and etiquette because of its vast territory and abundant resources\nB) The offending driver said to the traffic police, i have something urgent. i didn't see the traffic sign line clearly.\nC) The judge sentenced the defendant to ten years' imprisonment\nD) The weatherman on tv said: the highest temperature today is 24 degrees celsius and it is cloudy", '<think>.\nTo determine which statement contains a typical subtext, let\'s analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) "When giving a lecture, the history teacher said: China is a land of etiquette and etiquette because of its vast territory and abundant resources."This statement seems straightforward and doesn\'t contain any hidden meaning or implied opinion.\n\nB) "The offending driver said to the traffic police, \'I have something urgent.I didn\'t see the traffic sign line clearly.\'"This statement also appears to be clear and direct, without any hidden meaning or implied opinion.\n\nThe judge pardoned the defendant and granted them early release. This statement is ambiguous and may contain hidden meanings or implied opinions.\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
