messages:   25%|##5       | 152/600 [09:09<02:14,  3.34it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nNearly all employees of the factory who have completed their high school diploma have earned their factory safety certificate, having easily completed the eight week training course. The high school graduates who haven' t earned the certificate are ones who have evening obligations that have prevented them from taking the course. Overall, though, most of the factory workers have not earned the certificate.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, if the statements above are true, which one of the following also must be true?\n# Options:\nA) A large proportion of the factory workers have not graduated from high school.\nB) A large proportion of students with high school diplomas have evening obligations that have prevented them from taking the eight week training course.\nC) Most of the workers who have earned the certificate are high school graduates.\nD) No factory worker without a high school diploma has completed the course and earned the certificate.", "<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let's break down the information provided and analyze each option step by step.\n\n1.**Context Analysis:**.\n   - All employees with high school diplomas have earned their factory safety certificate.\n   - High school graduates without certificates have evening obligations preventing them from taking the course.\n   - Most factory workers have not earned the certificate.\n\n2.**Question:**.\n   - Which statement must be true based on the given information?.\n\n3.**Option A:**.\n   - A large proportion of the factory workers have not graduated from high school.\n   - This statement is not necessarily true.The context only mentions that high school graduates without certificates have evening obligations, but it does not provide 