messages:   29%|##9       | 175/600 [09:16<02:26,  2.90it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nDirectional movement refers to the directional motion caused by the external stimulation of plants in a single direction, including positive motion, gravity movement, tactile motion and directional motion. Most of the directional movement is growth movement, which is an irreversible process of motion.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options is a directional movement, as defined above?\n# Options:\nA) The puppy, lured repeatedly by the bone, sees the bone again and continues to droouff\nB) The roots of rice always grow in the direction of more fertilizer in the soil\nC) The petals of the cow spread in the morning, and when the sun shines directly at noon, the petals close\nD) Plants that prefer shade grow better in the shade than in direct sunlight', "<think>.\nTo determine which option represents a directional movement as defined in the context, let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) The puppy, lured repeatedly by the bone, sees the bone again and continues to droouff.\n- This option describes a behavior where the puppy is attracted to the bone and continues to move towards it.However, this is not a directional movement in the context of plants.It is a behavior driven by external stimuli (the bone) and not by the plant's internal response to environmental cues.\n\nB) The roots of rice always grow in the direction of more fertilizer in the soil.\n- This option describes a directional movement where the roots of rice grow towards areas with more fertilizer.This is a growth movement driven by the plant's response to an external stimulus (fertilizer).It fits the definition of directional movement as defined in the context.\n\nPlants that thrive in sunlight grow better in direct sunlight than in the shade.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
