messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nInvisible curriculum refers to the informal and unconscious learning experience that is not clearly specified in the school's planned curriculum.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the following is not an invisible curriculum?\n# Options:\nA) Colleges and universities organize students to participate in two-day military training to cultivate and exercise students' willpower.\nB) When children learn teaching courses, they cultivate their interest in learning and teaching.\nC) A university set up a university culture festival to let students know the school motto and style of study.\nD) Teachers and students participate in extracurricular activities together to establish an equal and harmonious relationship between teachers and students.", '<think>.\nTo determine which option is not an example of an invisible curriculum, let\'s analyze each option based on the definition provided:.\n\n1.**Option A**: "Colleges and universities organize students to participate in two-day military training to cultivate and exercise students\' willpower."This option describes a structured activity that aims to develop specific skills (willpower) through a formal educational setting.While it may have some educational value, it is not necessarily an example of an invisible curriculum because it is explicitly designed to teach a particular skill or trait.\n\n2.**Option B**: "When children learn teaching courses, they cultivate their interest in learning and teaching."This option suggests that children are learning about teaching as part of their curriculum, which implies that the interest in learning and teaching is being taught explicitly.Therefore, this does not fit the definition of an invisible curriculum.\n\n3.**Option C**: "A university set up a university culture festival to let students know the school motto and style of study."Based on this analysis, the option that is an example of an invisible curriculum is:. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
