s as the best treatment.\nThis option highlights the shift in treatment approaches for alcoholism, which is consistent with the argument that attitudes towards alcoholism have changed.However, it does not provide direct evidence for the increased reporting of alcohol-related deaths.\n\nIn some places and times, susceptibility to any kind of disease has never been viewed as a moral failing. This has no relevance to the current situation, where there is a decrease in reported deaths from alcohol-related conditions and a positive shift in attitudes towards alcoholism.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
