messages:   48%|####7     | 285/600 [10:25<03:15,  1.61it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nBroken window effect is a psychological phenomenon, that is, if the window of a house is broken and no one repair it, and soon other windows will also be broken.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which one of the followings does not belong to broken window effect?\n# Options:\nA) If the graffiti on a wall is not cleaned, the wall will soon be full of messy and ugly things.\nB) If a tributary is polluted and not treated, it may pollute the water quality of the whole basin.\nC) Once there is rubbish in a very clean place, people will throw their rubbish away without hesitation and will not feel ashamed.\nD) If a few people in a group speak uncivilized languages and are not stopped, many people will soon speak uncivilized languages.', "<think>.\nTo solve this problem, let's analyze each option based on the definition of the broken window effect.The broken window effect suggests that if something is damaged or neglected, it will lead to further damage or neglect.Let's examine each option:.\n\nA) If the graffiti on a wall is not cleaned, the wall will soon be full of messy and ugly things.\n- This option aligns with the broken window effect because if graffiti is not removed, it will likely attract more graffiti, leading to a more messy and ugly wall.\n\nB) If a tributary is polluted and not treated, it may pollute the water quality of the whole basin.\n- This option also fits the broken window effect.If a tributary is polluted, it could contaminate the entire basin, affecting the water quality of the whole area.\nIf a few people in a group speak uncivilized languages and are not stopped, many people will not soon speak uncivilized languages.\n- This option does not align with the broken window effect. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
