messages:   56%|#####6    | 337/600 [10:57<01:53,  2.32it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nRight to equality refers to the right of citizens to enjoy their rights equally without any unreasonable differential treatment and require equal protection from the state.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above rights, which of the followings is the violation of right to equality?\n# Options:\nA) In a divorce case, a woman asked for an equal division of the joint property of the husband and wife\nB) Women demand equal pay with men for equal work\nC) A primary school refused to accept students with physical disabilities\nD) A married daughter asked to inherit her father's inheritance with her brother", "<think>.\nTo determine which option violates the right to equality, we need to analyze each option individually and see if it involves differential treatment based on gender, disability, or other factors that could be considered discriminatory.\n\nA) In a divorce case, a woman asked for an equal division of the joint property of the husband and wife:.\nThis option does not involve any differential treatment based on gender.Both parties are seeking an equal division of their joint property, which is a fair and equitable approach.Therefore, this option does not violate the right to equality.\n\nB) Women demand equal pay with men for equal work:.\nThis option involves a demand for equal pay for equal work, which is a common issue related to the right to equality.Women are demanding equal pay for the same work as men, which is a form of differential treatment based on gender.This option violates the right to equality.\nA married daughter did not ask to inherit her father's inheritance with her brother, which is a situation free from any gender bias or discrimination.\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
