messages:   59%|#####8    | 353/600 [13:02<07:15,  1.76s/it][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIf absolute fairness is implemented, it will inevitably lead to distribution according to work; If distribution according to work, there will be inequality between the rich and the poor; Only by equalizing the rich and the poor can absolute fairness be implemented.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, so\n# Options:\nA) Distribution according to work must be implemented\nB) Distribution on demand must be implemented\nC) Absolute fairness must be implemented\nD) Can not implement absolute fairness', "<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let's break down the given statements and analyze them step by step:.\n\n1.**Statement 1:** If absolute fairness is implemented, it will inevitably lead to distribution according to work.\n   - This means that if absolute fairness is achieved, then distribution according to work must occur.\n\n2.**Statement 2:** If distribution according to work, there will be inequality between the rich and the poor.\n   - This implies that when distribution is based on work, there will be a disparity in wealth between those who work more and those who work less.\n\n3.**Statement 3:** Only by equalizing the rich and the poor can absolute fairness be implemented.\n   - This suggests that achieving absolute fairness requires addressing the issue of inequality between the rich and the poor.\n\nNow, let's consider the options:.\n\nA) Distribution according to work must be implemented.\n   - From Statement 1, we know that if absolute fairness is implemented, distribution according to work will occur.Therefore, this option is true.\n\nB) Distribution on demand must be implemented.The incorrect answer is B.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
