messages:   62%|######1   | 370/600 [13:09<01:05,  3.52it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIn recent years, as tourism exploration has become more and more popular by some people, there are more and more rescue operations. Should we charge for the deployment of public resources to rescue tourism explorers who commit intentional adventures? These issues have also become the topic that everyone is most concerned about. The positive side thinks that it should be charged; the opposite side thinks that it should not be charged.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following, if true, cannot support the positive side's point of view?\n# Options:\nA) A rational citizen should be responsible for his own actions; otherwise, it will be unfair to other taxpayers\nB) The establishment of a professional rescue system requires a certain amount of financial support\nC) It is the duty of government departments to rescue people in distress. simple charges can not help adventurers build up a sense of social responsibility\nD) Tourist explorers who illegally enter unsafe areas and waste social resources and taxpayers' money should bear the corresponding expenses", "<think>.\nTo determine which option cannot support the positive side's point of view, let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) A rational citizen should be responsible for his own actions; otherwise, it will be unfair to other taxpayers.\n- This option suggests that tourists should bear the cost of their own actions, including those that lead to rescue operations.This aligns with the idea of charging for the deployment of public resources to rescue tourists who commit intentional adventures.\n\nIt is not the duty of government departments to rescue people in distress.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
