n Tuesday or Wednesday.\n   - If C is on Wednesday, then A and D must be two days apart, which means A can be on Thursday or Friday.\n   - If C is on Friday, then A and D must be two days apart, which means A can be on Saturday or Sunday, but this is not possible since A is only on duty from Monday to Friday.\n\nConsidering the impossible days for A:\n- If C is on Monday, then A cannot be on Tuesday or Wednesday.\n- If C is on Wednesday, then A cannot be on Thursday or Friday.\n- If C is on Friday, then A cannot be on Saturday or Sunday, and this is indeed possible since A is on duty from Monday to Friday.\n\nCombining the misinformation:\n- If B is on Monday, C can be on Monday, so C cannot be on Wednesday or Friday.\n- If C is on Wednesday, then A cannot be on Thursday or Friday.\n- If C is on Friday, then A cannot be on Saturday or Sunday, and this is indeed possible since A is on duty from Monday to Friday.\n\nConclusion:\n- The only impossible scenario that contradicts all the constraints is when B is on Monday, C is on Wednesday, and A is on Thursday.\n\nTherefore, the incorrect answer is:. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
