es decide on complex civil trials, they have a better understanding of the complexity of those trials than the jury.\n   - This option is not supported by the context.The context does not mention anything about judges having a better understanding of complex trials than the jury.\n\n5.**Option C:**.\n   - The complexity of most civil trials exceeds the comprehension of the jury.The simplicity of most civil trials is well within the understanding of the jury.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
