the science class.Again, we don't have any information about the distribution of boys and girls within each class type.\n     - Therefore, we cannot conclude that this option is necessarily true based on the given information.\n\n   - **Option C:** The total number of boys in the liberal arts class is higher than that of girls in the science class.Based on the given information, all of the options A, B, C, or D can be definitively concluded as correct. The information provided is sufficient to determine the exact distribution of boys and girls within each class type.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
