cooled.\n   - Overall, adopting the new process will cost much but bring the company no profit.\n\n2.**Supervisor's Disagreement:**.\n   - The supervisor agrees with the overall conclusion that adopting the new process will cost much but bring the company no profit.\n   - However, the supervisor disagrees with the plant manager's statement that the new process is more expensive to run than the current process.\n\n3.**Analysis:**.\n   - The plant manager argues that the new process is more expensive to run because it requires reheating the cooled copper.The supervisor agrees with this point, stating that the latest closed furnaces are not fuel-efficient.\n\n4.**Conclusion:**.\n   - The supervisor's agreement is about the cost of running the new process, specifically regarding the fuel efficiency of the new furnaces.\n\nTherefore, the point about which the supervisor expresses agreement with the plant manager is:.\n\nC) Whether the new copper-smelting process is more expensive to run than the current process..\n<｜User｜>Please solve the logical reasoning problem\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
