s leads to improved mental well-being.\n\nB) Studies have shown that staying in an urban environment makes people more likely to feel tired and depressed.\nThis option contradicts the conclusion that proximity to water is beneficial for mental health.It suggests that urban environments, which are often associated with water bodies, may actually have negative effects on mental health.\n\nStudies have shown that remaining far away from aquatic environments can incite negative emotions and increase stress compared with green spaces.\nThis option contradicts the conclusion that proximity to water is advantageous for both body and mind. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
