nd the effectiveness of advertising are also crucial.\n     - Therefore, this option seems plausible.\n\n   - **Option B:** "Newspaper circulation is not attractive to advertisers.".\n     - This statement directly contradicts the context, which states that the newspaper\'s circulation is large but still failed due to unsatisfactory advertising revenue.\n     - Thus, this option is incorrect.\nRelying on advertising revenue to run a newspaper is conducive to the development of the newspaper industry, and it is a key factor for newspapers to strive for success.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
