messages:   88%|########7 | 525/600 [18:38<00:48,  1.54it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nWittgenstein was a student of Moore, a famous philosopher at Cambridge University. One day, philosopher Russell asked Moore, who is your best student? Moore said without hesitation: Wittgenstein. why? because among all the students, only he always showed a blank look when listening to the class, and there were always endless questions. later, Wittgenstein is more famous than Russell. Someone asked, why did Russell fall behind? Wittgenstein said: he has no problem.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, this paragraph is intended to illustrate that:\n# Options:\nA) Doubting and questioning are always the secret of success\nB) Curiosity is the internal driving force of research\nC) Appreciation is an important factor in success\nD) Finding problems is the premise of continuous progress', '<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the information provided and analyze it step by step:.\n\n1.**Context Analysis:**.\n   - Wittgenstein was a student of Moore.\n   - Moore was a famous philosopher at Cambridge University.\n   - Russell asked Moore who his best student was.\n   - Moore replied that Wittgenstein was his best student.\n   - Russell later became more famous than Wittgenstein.\n   - Wittgenstein said that Russell fell behind because he had no problems.\n\n2.**Question Analysis:**.\n   - The question asks us to identify the main point or theme of the paragraph based on the given information.\n\n3.**Identifying the Theme:**.\n   - The paragraph discusses the relationship between Wittgenstein and Moore, and how Wittgenstein\'s approach to learning and questioning led to his success.\n   - It mentions that Wittgenstein always showed a blank look and had endless questions, which indicates a high level of curiosity and critical thinking.\n   - The statement "he has no problem" implies that Wittgenstein did not have any issues or obstacles that hindered his progress.\n\nBased on the analysis, the paragraph primarily focuses on the insignificance of curiosity and questioning in achieving success.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
