\'s plane.\n- This option involves a considerable number of individuals (passengers) expressing their opinions on a specific topic (the safety of the airline\'s pilots).The opinions are related to public affairs (the safety of passengers) and are expressed by a considerable number of individuals.Therefore, this option fits the definition of public opinion.\n\nC) Li yong\'s relatives and friends unanimously praised the new house purchased by his family.This option involves a large number of individuals, groups, or organizations expressing their opinions on public affairs, not just a single individual expressing their opinion on a specific topic. Therefore, this option fits the definition of public opinion.\n\nA) Gao shan did not express different opinions on a decision of the company.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
