veyor's expectations.\n\n3.The question asks which possibility the reasoning in the researcher's argument overlooks.\n\n4.Option A suggests that a survey that disguises the surveyor's expectations might still be flawed in other ways unrelated to the surveyor's expectations.This aligns with the context, as the researcher acknowledges that well-constructed surveys can reduce bias, but does not mention other potential flaws.\n\n5.Option B suggests that some people who know what answers the surveyor expects to hear will purposefully try to thwart the surveyor's expectations.The researcher thoroughly examines the possibility that the answers of opinion-survey respondents can be influenced by beliefs about the surveyor's expectations, even if those beliefs are unfounded. This is acknowledged in the context, unlike what is stated in Option D.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
