sue of whether the bridge needs to be demolished and rebuilt.\n\nB) 99% of international ships entering the yangtze river are berthed at ports below nanjing bridge, and few large foreign ships are berthed at dozens of foreign trade docks above nanjing.\n- This option indicates that most international ships are not affected by the bridge's height, as they are already berthed at ports below the bridge.This suggests that the bridge's height is not a major obstacle for international shipping.\n\nC) Demolishing the Nanjing Bridge alone was sufficient. The Yangtze River bridges constructed in Wuhu, Tongling, Anqing, and other locations had a headroom height of 24 meters.\n- This option indicates that the Nanjing Yangtze River Bridge's height is a unique issue, as other bridges along the Yangtze River do not have similar heights.\n\nD) The shipbuilding technology is not very advanced, and the 8000-ton class ships designed for the Yangtze River have not been able to sail directly to Wuhan through Nanjing.\n- This option implies that the shipbuilding technology is not advanced enough to enable ships to pass under the bridge, especially if it is not tall enough.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
