conclude this option is necessarily true.\n   - **Option B:** The number of owners of private aircraft who use the county's airport facilities will not change appreciably in the future.\n     - This option assumes that the number of private aircraft owners using the airport will remain constant.The context does not provide any information about future trends or changes in the number of private aircraft owners.Therefore, we cannot conclude this option is necessarily true.\n   - **Option C:** Most of the county's citizens live a convenient distance from one or another airport now offering commercial airline services.Based on the context provided, it is clear that the airport's operating expenses were not greater than the revenue raised from sources other than the airport user fees for private planes. Therefore, this conclusion is false.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
